From 357c1482718e204909893e0c2b03634998de01bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Railgun-wiki <64968531+Railgun-wiki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:29:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo

Document sysfs platform ABI entries added for Mechrevo GM5HG0A and
compatible Uniwill laptop platforms, covering perf_mode, power_led_mode,
TDP power limits (tdp_spl, tdp_sppt, tdp_fppt), thermal limit (tcc_offset),
11-point binary fan curves (fan_curve1, fan_curve2), fan_boost,
discrete GPU power control (dgpu_power), and display MUX scheme (mux_scheme).

Signed-off-by: Railgun-wiki <64968531+Railgun-wiki@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo       | 115 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 115 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..737ebec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mechrevo
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/perf_mode
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		Platform performance mode selection. Reading returns the
+		current mode ("office", "gaming", "turbo", "custom", or "unknown").
+		Writing sets the mode register (EC 0x0751) and updates the
+		corresponding power LED indicators:
+		- "office": Power saving mode (EC 0xA0, LED mode 0)
+		- "gaming": Balanced / Gaming mode (EC 0x00, LED mode 1)
+		- "turbo": Maximum performance mode (EC 0x10, LED mode 2)
+		- "custom": User defined mode (EC 0x20, LED mode 1)
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/power_led_mode
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		Direct control of the multi-color power LED indicator (EC 0x07A5).
+		Reading returns the current LED mode index (0..3).
+		Writing applies an atomic read-modify-write on bits 1:0 of the
+		status register while strictly preserving the silent (bit 2) and
+		fan boost (bit 4) status bits.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_spl
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_spl_min
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_spl_max
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		AMD CPU Sustained Power Limit (SPL / PL1) in Watts.
+		Writing tdp_spl clamps the input value between tdp_spl_min
+		and tdp_spl_max and performs post-write readback verification
+		returning -EIO on failure.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_sppt
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_sppt_min
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_sppt_max
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		AMD CPU Slow Package Power Tracking limit (sPPT / PL2) in Watts.
+		Writing clamps the value within [tdp_sppt_min, tdp_sppt_max]
+		and verifies written value against EC register.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_fppt
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_fppt_min
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tdp_fppt_max
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		AMD CPU Fast Package Power Tracking limit (fPPT / PL4) in Watts.
+		Writing clamps the value within [tdp_fppt_min, tdp_fppt_max]
+		and verifies written value against EC register.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tcc_offset
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tcc_offset_min
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/tcc_offset_max
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		CPU Temperature Control Circuit (TCC) target ceiling in deg C.
+		Writing clamps the value between tcc_offset_min and tcc_offset_max
+		and asserts bit 7 as the hardware enable flag (EC 0x0786).
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/fan_curve1
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/fan_curve2
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		[UNVERIFIED]: Raw 11-point hardware fan table binary attributes
+		for CPU (fan_curve1) and GPU (fan_curve2) fan channels.
+		Fixed size: 33 bytes (11 points * 3 bytes).
+		Layout per point: {u8 up_temp_c, u8 down_temp_c, u8 duty_percent}.
+		Reading fetches live table from EC (0x0F00/0x0F30). Writing programs
+		all 11 points directly into EC fan registers.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/fan_boost
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		One-key fan boost (maximum speed) control.
+		Reading returns 1 if boost is active, 0 otherwise.
+		Writing 1 or 0 toggles bit 4 of EC status register 0x07A5.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/dgpu_power
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		[UNVERIFIED: REBOOT PREFERRED]: Discrete GPU PCIe slot power control.
+		Reading calls ACPI AMW0.OEMG(0x0300, 2) and returns 1 if powered
+		(0xAA) or 0 if cut (0x55).
+		Writing 0 invokes OEMG(0x0300, 1) cutting PCIe slot power; writing 1
+		invokes OEMG(0x0300, 0) restoring power.
+		WARNING: Userspace MUST unbind GPU kernel driver and remove the PCIe
+		device before writing 0. On GM5HG0A platforms, switching graphics
+		modes is designed to take effect after system reboot (via MUX NVRAM).
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/tuxedo_keyboard/mux_scheme
+Date:		September 2026
+KernelVersion:	6.1
+Contact:	OpenMechrevo Authors <dev@openmechrevo.org>
+Description:
+		Display MUX NVRAM variable scheme. Returns "amd" (0=MSHybrid, 1=dGPU,
+		2=iGPU), "intel" (4=MSHybrid, 2=dGPU, 1=iGPU), or "none" on platforms
+		without physical display MUX switching hardware. Automatically hidden
+		on motherboards without discrete graphics.
